  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 250 PM CST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\nBy Friday, the system ejects off to the northeast, and clouds clear \nout nicely for much of the day. Surface winds eventually shift to \nthe southwest, and we will warm back to near-normal temperatures \nwith highs in the upper 40s to low 50s for most. We return to a \nzonal upper air pattern for a couple of days, and highs soar into \nthe upper 50s to near 60 on Saturday. Another trough approaches\nSaturday night, however, bringing rain chances to much of the \narea with higher chances in central Missouri. This system may \nbring another tenth of an inch or two to areas in the eastern \nOzarks and central Missouri, but timing and amounts are still \nuncertain.\n\nTemperatures take a small dip Sunday in the wake of the trough, and \novernight lows will be especially chilly once again, but another \ncouple of days of zonal flow are expected to begin next week which \nallow another slight warm-up. The synoptic pattern looks to remain \nactive in the long term, though, so we are definitely not out of the \nwoods to begin December.",
